The Leiden Institute of Advanced Computer Science ( LIACS ) is looking for an excellent Post-doc researcher (1.0 FTE) with a background in Computer Science (or a closely related field) to join a project focused on developing an advanced machine learning framework for spatio-temporal datasets. The position is for 2.5 years and is partially funded by the Dutch Research Council (NWO) through the Aspasia premium awarded to dr. Mitra Baratchi for her research on machine learning for spatio-temporal data. The successful applicant will be embedded in the Spatio-temporal Data Analysis and Reasoning ( STAR ) and the Automated Design of Algorithms ( ADA ) research groups. Moreover, there are plenty of opportunities for interaction and collaboration with other groups at the institute and internationally.
The research is broadly focused on automated intervention design. An intervention is any external interference in an ongoing process that is performed to achieve a particular outcome. Being able to answer interventional questions automatically will help decision-makers solve complex challenges (i.e., reducing methane emissions or reducing the infection rate during a pandemic). Most machine learning algorithms designed for spatio-temporal data do not allow assessing the impact of interventions without capturing causal links. In this project, we aim to design algorithmic solutions grounded in causality for the automatic and scalable assessment of interventions using observational spatio-temporal datasets generated by modern sensing technologies (e.g., IoT sensors, mobile devices, Earth observations).
 What you will do 
Within this position, it is expected that you will:
 conduct research within the scope of the project leading to peer-reviewed publications in journals and conference proceedings;
 collaborate closely with Dr. Elena Raponi (the Natural Computing Group) and dr. Saber Salehkaleybar (the Explanatory Data Analysis Group) at LIACS;
 contribute to the teaching activities of the STAR Research Group and supervision of BSc and MSc students.
 Where you will work 
Curiosity and passion for science are what connect our people: we seek to know, understand, interpret, and create. Our mission is to provide excellent education and research across the full spectrum of the natural sciences, contributing to solutions for major societal challenges. Our eight institutes—ranging from mathematics, computer science, astronomy, physics, chemistry, and biopharmaceutical sciences to biology and environmental sciences—together with the Lorentz Center and the Hortus botanicus, form the backbone of our faculty and are closely connected. We work in a safe, stimulating, and international environment where enthusiasm and passion drive both research and education, and where building connections and collaboration, both within and beyond the faculty, come naturally.
The faculty is home to more than 2,700 staff members and over 6,000 students enrolled in nine bachelor's and fifteen master's programs. We are located at the heart of the Bio Science Park, one of Europe’s largest science parks, where academia and industry come together.
You will be part of the Leiden Institute of Advanced Computer Science (LIACS). LIACS offers the bachelor's programs in Computer Science and Data Science/Artificial Intelligence, as well as master's programs in Computer Science, ICT in Business and the Public Sector, Media Technology, and Science Based Business. According to an independent research assessment, LIACS is one of the leading computer science departments in the Netherlands. We strive for excellence in a supportive institute where academic achievement, enjoyment, and diversity go hand in hand. We offer a clear and welcoming career path for young and talented scientists with the ambition to grow. For more information about LIACS, visit our website.
 What you bring 
We are looking for a candidate with expertise or experience with one or more of the following topics: machine learning for spatio-temporal data, causal machine learning (casual discovery and causal inference), and automated machine learning.
 holding (or close to acquiring) a PhD degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence or a closely related field;
 strong research vision and an academic mindset;
 strong publication record;
 being able to collaborate with scientific peers inside and outside your own research area;
 strong programming skills in Python or other programming languages;
 excellent proficiency and communication skills in English.
 What we offer 
 A full-time 2,5 year position for initially one year. After a positive evaluation of the progress of the thesis, personal capabilities and compatibility the appointment will be extended by another 1,5 year. This contract falls under the CLA of Dutch Universities;
 A salary between € 3.546,= and € 5.538,= gross per month, based on a full-time appointment (38 hours, Payscale 10);
 A holiday allowance (8%), an end-of-year bonus (8,3%

academictransfer:363192.description:
The GeoLab is the central laboratory of the Faculty of Geosciences, where highly diverse research into the system Earth is conducted, often by using advanced analytical instruments. As analytical chemical technician for water analysis, you strengthen our team by analyzing the chemical composition of various types of water samples.
 Your job 
The GeoLab is divided into several lab units, each with its own expertise. In the water lab, you analyze the chemical composition of various types of water samples like, for example, freshwater, seawater and porewater. For the analysis, you make use of an ion chromatograph, a discrete analyzer for the spectrophotometric determination of, for example, macronutrients and a DOC analyzer for the measurement of dissolved carbon compounds. You conduct analyses for our students, scientists and sometimes external customers and report the processed results. You are responsible for the proper functioning of the equipment and the quality control of the measurements.
Research is constantly evolving and requires new or adapted methods. With your knowledge of the chemistry of complex solutions (i.e. seawater and porewater matrices), you will develop methods in cooperation with research faculty for the available analytical instruments that meet the need of the researchers better, and are preferably also more sustainable. Additionally, you advise lab users (e.g., students) on sample collection and pretreatment where necessary.
You work primarily in the water lab, where you will be supported by colleagues from the experimental lab. Vice versa, we expect you to be able to support your colleagues there as well when necessary. In the experimental lab, very diverse research is conducted on geological materials and environmental samples. Some examples of these experiments include reactions of organic compounds under conditions comparable to those on Mars and the release of phosphate from sediments under different circumstances. Within the experimental lab, we have a microbiology lab, cleanrooms and climate chambers available. Your contribution here will be primarily facilitative.
Preferably, you are already familiar with Emergency Response (in Dutch BHV) or are willing to become an Emergency Responder to strengthen our BHV team in the lab.
Your tasks include:
 You analyze the chemical composition of water samples using the analytical instruments available and report the processed data;
 You are responsible for the quality control of the measurements and the proper functioning of the instruments. This includes the preparation and use of standards and reagents. You can conduct daily maintenance independently;
 You develop new or modified methods together with researchers and can advise them about sample collection and pretreatment where necessary;
 You work closely together with your colleagues by supporting each other;
 You support fieldwork and lab courses and their preparation;
 Preferably, you are willing to act as an Emergency Responder in the event of an emergency.

REQUIREMENTS:
We are looking for a motivated and particularly proactive thinking and flexible technician who enjoys working in a dynamic environment with varying research questions. Furthermore, we require the following from you:
 You have a higher professional education (BSc) in Analytical Chemistry or equivalent, or you have otherwise gained relevant experience, preferentially in the field of water analysis. Experience in the analysis of environmental and ecological samples is a benefit;
 You work and think independently and support scientists and students by thinking along with them;
 You are good at performing troubleshooting on equipment; technical insight and logical thinking are essential;
 You are proficient in working with Excel;
 You have preferably demonstrable experience in developing analytical methods;
 You work carefully, in an orderly manner and independently, but you are also a good team player;
 You possess excellent communication skills enabling you to address various stakeholders (scientists, students, and external clients) in both Dutch and English. We expect foreign candidates to master the Dutch language within two years;
 You are willing to act as an Emergency Responder in the event of a dangerous situation and obtain and keep the necessary certificates up to date.

academictransfer:363196.description:
Het GeoLab is het centrale laboratorium van de Faculteit Geowetenschappen waar zeer divers onderzoek naar het systeem Aarde – vaak met behulp van geavanceerde analytische apparatuur – wordt uitgevoerd. Als analytisch-chemisch analist voor wateranalyse kom je ons team versterken door de chemische samenstelling van allerlei verschillende watermonsters te analyseren.
 Wat ga je doen? 
Het GeoLab is ingedeeld in meerdere labunits met ieder zijn eigen expertise. In het waterlab analyseer je de chemische samenstelling van verschillende soorten watermonsters. Dit kunnen bijvoorbeeld monsters van oppervlaktewater, zeewater en poriewater zijn. Voor de analyse maak je gebruik van een ion chromatograaf, een discrete analyzer voor bijvoorbeeld de spectrofotometrische bepaling van macronutriënten en een DOC analyzer voor het meten van opgeloste koolstofverbindingen. Je voert de analyses voor onze studenten, wetenschappers en soms ook externe opdrachtgevers uit en rapporteert de uitgewerkte meetresultaten. Je bent verantwoordelijk voor het goed functioneren van de aanwezige apparatuur en de kwaliteitscontrole van de metingen.
Het onderzoek ontwikkelt zich voortdurend en vraagt om nieuwe of aangepaste methodes. Met je kennis van de chemie van complexe oplossingen (zoals zeewater en poriewatermatrices) ontwikkel je in afstemming met de wetenschappers methodes voor de aanwezige analyseapparatuur die nog beter aansluiten aan de behoefte van de onderzoekers en bij voorkeur ook duurzamer zijn. Daarnaast adviseer je de labgebruikers (bijvoorbeeld studenten) over monstername en -voorbewerking waar nodig.
Je werkt voornamelijk in het waterlab waar je ondersteund wordt door collega’s van het experimentele lab. Andersom verwachten we van je dat je ook daar je collega’s kan ondersteunen als dit nodig is. In het experimentele lab wordt aan de hand van de meest uiteenlopende experimenten heel gevarieerd onderzoek verricht op geologisch materiaal en milieumonsters. Enkele voorbeelden zijn reacties van organische verbindingen onder vergelijkbare condities als op Mars en het vrijkomen van fosfaat uit waterbodems onder verschillende omstandigheden. Binnen de experimentele labunit hebben we een microbiologisch lab, cleanrooms en klimaatkamers ter beschikking. Jouw bijdrage hier zal voornamelijk faciliterend zijn.
Bij voorkeur ben je al bekend met bedrijfshulpverlening (BHV) of ben je bereid om bedrijfshulpverlener te worden om ons BHV team op het lab te versterken.
Je taken zijn onder andere:
 Je analyseert de chemische samenstelling van watermonsters met behulp van de aanwezige analyseapparatuur in het waterlab en rapporteert de door jou uitgewerkte resultaten;
 Je bent verantwoordelijk voor de kwaliteitscontrole van de metingen en het goed functioneren van de apparatuur. Dit omvat de bereiding en het gebruik van standaarden en reagentia. Dagelijks onderhoud kan je zelfstandig uitvoeren;
 Je ontwikkelt samen met de onderzoekers nieuwe of aangepaste methodes en kan ze over monstername en -voorbewerking adviseren waar nodig;
 Je werkt nauw samen met je collega’s door elkaar te ondersteunen;
 Je ondersteunt bij veldwerken en practica en de voorbereiding daarvan;
 Bij voorkeur ben je bereid als BHV-er in een geval van een calamiteit te handelen.

REQUIREMENTS:
We zijn op zoek naar een gemotiveerde en vooral meedenkende en flexibele analist die graag in een dynamische omgeving werkt met variërende onderzoeksvragen. Verder vragen wij van je dat:
 Je een analytisch-chemische HBO-opleiding of gelijkwaardig hebt of anderzijds relevante ervaring hebt opgedaan, bij voorkeur op het gebied van wateranalyse. Ervaring met de analyse van milieu en ecologische samples is een pre;
 Je een zelfstandig werk- en denkniveau hebt en je wetenschappers en studenten ondersteunt door met ze mee te denken;
 Je goed bent in het uitvoeren van troubleshooting op apparatuur; technisch inzicht en logisch denken zijn essentieel;
 Je vaardig bent in het werken met Excel;
 Je bij voorkeur al aantoonbare ervaring met het ontwikkelen van analysemethoden hebt opgedaan.
 Je zorgvuldig, ordelijk en zelfstandig werkt maar ook een goede teamplayer bent;
 Je over uitstekende communicatieve vaardigheden beschikt waarmee je verschillende stakeholders (wetenschappers, studenten en externe klanten) in zowel het Nederlands als in het Engels te woord kunt staan;
 Je bereid bent om in een geval van een gevaarlijke situatie als bedrijfshulpverlener te acteren en de hiervoor nodige certificaten behaalt en up-to-date houdt.

academictransfer:363198.description:
Are you passionate about developing cutting-edge AI techniques to enhance interaction and communication across multiple modalities, such as text, pictures, audio, and video? Join the large scale HAICu project to help unlock the potential of cultural digital archives through multimodal use, providing richer context and a more comprehensive analysis of current complex issues in society. If this fits your expertise and interests, the Interaction Division of Utrecht University is seeking you!
 Your job 
We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher to work within the multi-partner HAICu NWA-ORC project. This project is implemented by an ambitious consortium including many universities, knowledge institutions, archives, foundations, cultural institutions and business partners in the Netherlands. It aims to use improved access to digital heritage to tutor the Digital Citizen in the use of big data. It brings together AI researchers and Digital Humanities scholars to seek solutions to the problem of inadequate data-mining tools we have, aiming to derive information from the continuous stream of data about the present and the past. This will help citizens and other regular users, heritage curators and journalists who are interested in tapping heritage collections, as well as civic organizations and authorities interested in improving civic participation.
The research in this postdoctoral position focuses on text and image feature learning for news ecosystems, analysing the complex multidimensional feature space of visual information to support data-driven journalism. This includes experiments for accountability, transparency, inclusiveness, and misinformation. The key technology is multimodal deep learning, and its extensions for these additional targets. In particular, we have a large collection of newspaper articles dealing with migration-related topics, and we are investigating how text and image analysis can provide insights into such a corpus.
Research will include testing, validation and evaluation on large scale and interoperable collections, in cooperation with the societal partners in the project, including the Netherlands Institute for Sound and Vision, the National Archive, and the National Library of the Netherlands. The research will take place in collaboration with the HAICu fieldlab ‘Deep Journalism’, which develops functionality for searching for items about a similar topic from different archives and with various modalities to support news journalists.
As a postdoc in this project, you will conduct research in close collaboration with a multidisciplinary research team. This position offers you the opportunity to further develop your academic skills and contribute to groundbreaking research. Next to that it provides a unique opportunity to network with an extensive scientific and cultural network of people in the Netherlands, and to seek answers to societal problems jointly with a great team of top scholars.

REQUIREMENTS:
We are looking for a talented postdoc candidate, with a keen interest in academic and professional development, who meets the following requirements:
 a PhD degree in computer science or artificial intelligence;
 demonstrable machine learning skills;
 curiosity about societal issues and how AI can be employed for the benefit of the public;
 strong teamwork skills, as collaboration with other researchers and stakeholders is key to the project’s success;
 comfortable in doing multidisciplinary research and interacting with important stakeholders and eager to conduct innovative and thorough research;
 fluency in written and spoken English.

